ctedtoanything|connectedto anything|connected toanything\" \"loose ?ends|looseends\"; do n=$(grep -E \"^   item \" $L | grep -ciE \"$p\"); echo \"$n  $p\"; done","timeout":30000,"description":"Count Error List items per class from the read log"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_015c5Kt2t2po1MdBmchur4Yf","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\" && py tools/bgrun.py --max-min 10 --log tools/bench/retro.log -- py tools/retrospective.py --cycle 110","timeout":660000,"description":"Run cycle 110 retrospective under bgrun"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJnc4G528SuBwMRJhsDvrL","tool_input":{"command":"F=\"C:/Users/KimLab/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/G--Codes-LabVIEW-Codes-MinLab-zz-LabView-VI-AAA-UNIST-2--Tracking-V6-ParallelLoop/d15e585c-0516-4520-9ba8-22cc4f749a87/tasks/b1uc0upqe.output\"; for i in $(seq 1 110); do grep -qE \"BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT)\" \"$F\" && break; sleep 5; done; grep -E \"BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT)|VIOLATION|archived\" \"$F\"","timeout":600000,"description":"Block until the retrospective ends (≤ 9 min)"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q3BNT8PeQo52yrAXX3xD9G","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\" && py tools/violations.py --due; echo rc=$?; py tools/protocol.py validate tools/bench/next.json","timeout":30000,"description":"Check violation decisions parse and next.json"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":4,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":4,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":4,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":3,"material-opus-max":1}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":77,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 110 is finished. The display-loop VI is accepted: it ran the experiment with almost no lost frames, and its X/Y/Z output is identical to the original's on the same recorded frames. L2-B1 was built and saved but is not yet the working VI: its Error List was only partly read.\n\n**Display-loop VI (`D1_s1_disp_20260927_041648.vi`)**\n- **Real run** (4 runs, original copy / new / new / original copy, 15 beads, 90 Hz): the original copy lost **3,359 and 5,860** frames; the display-loop VI lost **16 and 12**.\n  - All 15 bead picks registered in every run, and the rotor port opened normally on every run.\n  - The pass rule was fixed before the numbers were taken: both new-VI runs had to lose fewer than 2,207 frames, which they did by a wide margin.\n- **Recorded-frame replay** (the check that the computation is unchanged): X/Y/Z are **bit-identical on all 4,443 rows** the two runs share.\n  - The only differences are the live motor readback columns and the save-time bytes at the end of the calibration file, the same exclusions as the cycle-78 check.\n  - In the same time the new VI tracked 8,548 frames, against 4,443 for the original.\n- **Recorded:** acceptance written as plan decision 224(d); requirement R4 (no frame loss at 15 beads) is now marked as moving in the goal map.\n- This is the first VI in the project that runs an experiment with fewer lost frames than the original. It stays on the side branch and is not used in experiments until you say so.\n\n**Pre-run checker false alarm:** one of the offline pre-run checks (X9) wrongly blocked the replay build. It now only checks steps the build script actually executes (self-test 8/0).\n\n**L2-B1** (the first part of moving the tracking group into loop 1.2)\n- **Saved:** `D1_l2_b1_20260927_193100.vi` (md5 `b705728a…`). All 27 build steps matched the simulation.\n- **Not yet the working VI:**\n  - The Error List reader stops at 80 items and this VI has 99, so the expected-error file could not be written.\n  - One new wire (#11261 → #8323) is broken in the saved file, and I don't yet know why. Either it is waiting on input rows that the next two build steps will wire, or it wrongly crosses between loops.\n- The working VI stays `D1_l2_a3_20260927_151224.vi` until that is settled.\n\n**Retrospective:** one fault, which I accepted. The offline dry run, built to list every broken row in one go, stopped early. Two dead rows then took one extra Opus-max session to find (about 13 min). The fix is decided and recorded.\n\n**Next cycle (111)**, in `tools/bench/next.json` and STATUS NEXT:\n1. Read the full Error List of L2-B1, including the item(s) on that wire and which loop each end sits in. B1 becomes the working VI only if every item is accounted for.\n2. Fix the dry run so it reports every broken row in one pass, and apply the rule that `py -m <module>` is not a script launch on all three check paths (fixed on only one so far).\n3. Then plan L2-B2 offline.\n\nNo new questions for you. Still pending from before: `.claude/agents/material.md:61-62` tells sessions to use the `MATERIAL=1` prefix, which the permission layer refuses. The replacement text is in `tools/bench/audit_c7_agent_patch.md`, but only you can make that edit.\n\nThe Figma connector needs authorizing in your claude.ai connector settings; until then this session cannot use it.","ttft_ms":2115,"type":"result","duration_ms":10121104,"uuid":"c3b0b990-2093-4b9e-ad1c-66e4f1e4b2e0","ttft_stream_ms":1869,"time_to_request_ms":255,"first_content_frame_ms":1869,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
